<!--
    kuna `gotonext`: a `goto` whose target is the statement that runs next
    anyway is left out (upstream `BlockGoto::gotoPrints`), a `goto` to the
    statement after the innermost enclosing loop or switch prints as
    `break;`, and the label only those gotos reached goes with them.  A switch
    case that is a `BlockGoto` to another case chains to it, so the case sort
    places the target right after it and the jump becomes a fall-through.

    Stage / sub-stage: P8 "goto-quality".  The P0 assertion
    `option gotonext on|off` decides the rendering; on is the default.

    The bytes are decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/gotonext.c
    built at -O2 -fno-pie -no-pie -nostartfiles (x86-64 SysV): gcc 15.3 at
    0x401000 (fall, arith, strcase) and clang 22.1 linked at 0x501000
    (fall_clang).  fall has case fall-throughs, arith one case that leaves the
    switch, strcase a loop exit to the outer loop's next iteration.

    Pass 1 runs with no option line, the shipped default (on).  Pass 2
    (`option gotonext off`) reproduces the gotos.
-->
